| Critical | The ESP32 laser protocol and the Raspberry Pi laser controller are separate implementations. The rover uses `LaserController` on Pi GPIO 18, while the firmware expects ESP32 GPIO 4. The configuration says GPIO 25.  | [rover_main.py](https://github.com/BayazidHabibSiddikee/Semi-Autonomous-Weeding-Robot/blob/main/Navigation/src/rover_main.py?utm_source=chatgpt.com), [laser_control.py](https://github.com/BayazidHabibSiddikee/Semi-Autonomous-Weeding-Robot/blob/main/Weed_Detection/src/laser_control.py?utm_source=chatgpt.com)              |
| Critical | The safety check can return `True` when GPIO support is unavailable and the application is not in simulation mode. That is a fail-open condition.                                                                      | [laser_control.py](https://github.com/BayazidHabibSiddikee/Semi-Autonomous-Weeding-Robot/blob/main/Weed_Detection/src/laser_control.py?utm_source=chatgpt.com)                                                                                                                                                                    |
